    w("")
    w("## 7. C5 - the column-sensing decision")
    w("")
    w(f"Digital cost (1E, g = 8, measured): 160 columns at once {cm['reads_160']:,.0f} reads / {c5['rows'][0]['cycles']:,.0f} cycles; 20 at a time 428,717 / 837,745. The 1E cycle counts fit **cycles = {cm['c0']:,.0f} + group reads** to within {cm['c0_spread']:.0f} cycles over all seven 1E runs (g = 4..64 at 160 columns, 20 columns at g = 8 and 64): "
      "one cycle per group read on top of ingest. So for any width W (passes = ceil(160/W)) the cycle count follows. Electrical side: the five-macro DC study, plus crosstalk transients for the bit-plane mode (`column_sensing_table.json`, `crosstalk_bitplane_raw.json`).")
    w("")
    rows = []
    for r_ in c5["rows"]:
        if r_["rho"] != C.RAIL_R_DEFAULT:
            continue
        rows.append([r_["W"], r_["mode"], r_["passes"], f"{r_['reads']:,.0f}", f"{r_['cycles']:,.0f}", f"{r_['i_total_near_mA']:.1f}", f"{r_['dyn_far_a']*1e6:.3f}", f"{u(r_['margin_left_a'])} ({100*r_['margin_frac']:+.1f}%)", "yes" if r_["closes"] else f"NO (closes from {r_['earliest_closing_sampling_ps']} ps)"])
    w(md_table(["columns sensed at once", "mode", "passes", "group reads / inference", "cycles / inference", "peak current, near group (mA)", "dynamic error at 200 ps (uA)", "budget margin", "closes at 200 ps"], rows))
    w("")
    w("- **160 at once is electrically viable and has the lowest cycle count**; every contiguous-macro width closes with the same ~0.5 uA margin: the supply/ground rails (at 0.0072 ohm/pitch, both ends) are not the limit. The limit would be rail quality: at 0.072 ohm/pitch even a single macro fails (section 4.2); that, not the number of columns, is what sets the largest viable width.")
    w("- **The bit-plane (20-column) mode is the worst electrical option**, not the safe one. Un-sensed bitlines are either floating - then they charge toward V_read through the cells that hang on the driven row line (LRS cells in ~150 ps, HRS cells in ~20 ns), drawing transient current through the shared row line and driver: "
      f"a data-dependent error of {c5['rows'][-2]['dyn_far_a']*1e6:.1f} uA at 200 ps even without coupling (cc 0: 2.2 uA at G = 0), and the budget closes only from {c5['rows'][-2]['earliest_closing_sampling_ps']} ps - or clamped to ground, which turns every idle cell into a DC load: each of the 8 reads then draws the full 160-column current, **8x the array energy** for the same result.")
    w("- **Decision: sense all 160 columns simultaneously (five macros, one pass).** Largest viable simultaneous width measured: **160** (no electrical limit reached; peak supply current {:.0f} mA at 0.1 V = {:.1f} mW for the nanosecond of the pulse, which is what the decoupling of section 5.1 has to deliver).".format(c5["rows"][0]["i_total_near_mA"], c5["rows"][0]["i_total_near_mA"] * 0.1))
    w("")
    w("## 8. Energy and latency for Phase 5")
    w("")
    w("### 8.1 Energy per inference, from 1E's read pattern")
    w("")
    w(f"1E issues one group read per (non-skipped count bit-row, group); the active rows a of each read is the popcount of the 8 count bits there. Phase 0's golden count vectors (240 DVS-Gesture samples) give that pattern exactly: **{en['reads_issued_per_inference']:,.0f} reads issued per inference, "
      f"of which {en['nonzero_reads_per_inference']:,.0f} have a > 0 ({100*(1-en['zero_read_fraction']):.0f}%), mean a = {en['mean_active_rows_per_nonzero_read']:.2f} rows per non-zero read, {en['active_row_reads_per_inference']:,.0f} active-row reads in total.** "
      "Energy = sum over reads of 5 x V_read x I_macro(G, a) x (T - tau) + a x 5 x C_WL x V_WL^2, with I_macro from the validated mesh (baseline rails, both-end drive, random weights), tau the pulse-start loss measured in the transients, and zero for a = 0 reads (no row is driven).")
    w("")
    w(md_table(["pulse length T", "array (nJ)", "word line (nJ)", "total (nJ / inference)", "per issued read (pJ)", "per non-zero read (pJ)", "% of NeuroHDC-small 3.01 uJ"],
               [[f"{float(T)*1e9:g} ns", f"{d['array_J']*1e9:.1f}", f"{d['wordline_J']*1e9:.1f}", f"{d['total_J']*1e9:.1f}", f"{d['per_issued_read_pJ']:.3f}", f"{d['per_nonzero_read_pJ']:.2f}", f"{d['total_J']/3.01e-6*100:.1f}%"] for T, d in en["energy_per_inference_J"].items()]))
    w("")
    w("These are the array only: the sense front-ends (input stage, comparators, reference DACs), the ladder-table and gain-correction memories' read energy, the row-driver and word-line buffer short-circuit/leakage, and the digital 1E blocks are not included. The pulse length T is set by the sense stage (not designed in 1C): "
      "the energy is linear in it, **so the sense stage's required integration time is the first number Phase 5 needs.** Energy is independent of g (it is set by the active-row reads); it depends on whether idle bitlines are clamped (section 7).")
    w("")
    w("### 8.2 Latency per group read")
    w("")
    w(f"Array: **0.13-0.16 ns** to settle to 0.1 uA (worst group, a = 8 or 4) and the crosstalk is below 0.1 uA from ~150 ps; sampling at 200 ps loses nothing (section 4.4). The comparator/ladder decision time [not designed] and the word-line rise (the next group's word lines can be raised during the current read; "
      f"58 fF at 1.1 V, ~60 ps with a 1 kohm buffer [ASSUM]) are additional. At NeuroHDC's 100 MHz clock a group read fits in a cycle with a factor ~50 to spare, which is why the cycle count (**{c5['rows'][0]['cycles']:,.0f} per inference = events + 1 cycle per group read**) rather than the array latency sets the inference time.")
    w("")
