    w("")
    w("## 10. Handoff to 1D (write path)")
    w("")
    w("What the full-array work reveals for programming (the write itself is not simulated in 1C; 1B's write assumptions 10 pJ per pulse, 3 verify retries [ASSUM] are used only for scale):")
    w("")
    w(f"- **Rails and drivers are sized for read currents of ~70 mA; a row-parallel SET is the same order.** 160 cells x ~280 uA (the 20 F^2 ideal drive from 1A) = 45 mA per row if the whole row is set at once, 4.5 mA per driver (two per macro row): ~45 mV across a 10 ohm driver, small against a ~1-2 V SET, "
      "but R_DRV and the strap are **dimensioned for 0.1 V reads**: the write voltage path (driver type, rail voltage) is a 1D decision that the read-sized drivers do not settle.")
    w("- **Idle bitlines are not free.** A floating bitline is pulled toward the row potential through every cell on it (section 7): during a write the un-selected columns of the selected row must be held at the right potential by a clamp, otherwise they follow the row voltage on a ~150 ps (LRS) to ~20 ns (HRS) time constant and the *write disturb* depends on the neighbours' state; "
      "a clamp turns them into DC loads (current = row voltage / (R_dev + R_tx)) and that current is the programming current through the shared rail that 1D must budget.")
    w(f"- **Full-array program time and energy at 1B's assumptions:** {C.FULL_CELLS*C.ROWS_TOTAL*2:,} devices x 3 pulses x 10 pJ = {C.FULL_CELLS*C.ROWS_TOTAL*2*3*10e-12*1e6:.1f} uJ (1B: 4.9 uJ per refresh of the 163,840 devices); time = pulses x pulse width / parallelism: with a 100 ns pulse [ASSUM] row-parallel (320 devices per pulse) {C.ROWS_TOTAL*2*3*100e-9*1e3:.2f} ms, device-serial {C.FULL_CELLS*C.ROWS_TOTAL*2*3*100e-9*1e3:.0f} ms.")
