    w("| 'the row-line gain is correctable by a per-column ladder scale' | it varies with the group: a per-column scale leaves ~5% (7% with rails); rank 2-3 correction needed (section 3.3). |")
    w("| 'centre tap: g* 8 -> 16 at sigma <= 0.05' (0.72 ohm/pitch) | holds at 0.5 ohm/pitch (to ~0.054) but only to ~0.022 at 0.72; the lumped model understated the within-group wire term 2.2x. Segmented-with-middle-node gives ~0.048 at 0.72. |")
    w("| 'whether 160 columns sense at once turns on droop and crosstalk' | it does not: both are small; what decides it is the idle-bitline behaviour of the narrow mode. |")
    w("| g = 8 margin 0.80 uA (6.4%) | 0.48 uA (3.9%) with the 1C terms; marginal. |")
    w("")
    w("## 12. Honest limits")
    w("")
    w("- The 1B and 1C margins (0.8 / 0.48 uA) are within the budget's Monte-Carlo and pattern-sampling error (a few percent of the limit): treat g = 8 as marginal. The data-dependent terms use 8 own x 40 other draws (maximum of a standard deviation over own patterns), and the gain-correction residual is near the sampling floor of its estimate (~0.05%).")
    w("- Transients assume an ideal supply at the rail pads, a linear access transistor (no charge injection), word line asserted before the pulse, no sense stage; the bitline/row/rail capacitances are the related-work 0.2 fF/pitch [ASSUM]. The pad network (R_pad 0.5 ohm, L_pad 100 pH) of the supply-dynamics study is assumed; its trend (ringing delays the usable sampling time, no data dependence) is the result, not the numbers.")
